#. +> trunk6 stable6
#: advanced.docbook:461
#, no-c-format
msgid "&quot;Buckle!&quot; you think, it is of course <classname>MyClass</classname>. You go to line 3902, and instead of trying to find the word in the text, you launch the Editing Command Dialog, enter <userinput>s/myclass/MyClass/i</userinput>, hit the <guibutton>OK</guibutton> button, save the file and compile &ndash; successfully without the error."
msgstr "E de seguida lle chega a iluminación: «Claro! O nome correcto é <classname>UnhaClase</classname>». Vai á liña 3902, e en vez de intentar atopar a palabra no texto, inicia o diálogo de orde de edición, insire <userinput>s/unhaclase/UnhaClase/i</userinput>, preme Intro, garda o ficheiro e volve lanzar o compilador: «correctamente sen o erro»."

#. Tag: title
#. +> trunk6 stable6
#: advanced.docbook:471
#, no-c-format
msgid "Replacing text in the whole file"
msgstr "Substitución de texto en todo o ficheiro"

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk6 stable6
#: advanced.docbook:473
#, no-c-format
msgid "Imagine that you have a file, in which you mention a <quote>Miss Jensen</quote> several times, when someone comes in and tells you that she just got married to <quote>Mr Jones</quote>. You want, of course, to replace each and every occurrence of <quote>Miss Jensen</quote> with <quote>Ms Jones</quote>."
msgstr "Imaxine que ten un ficheiro no que menciona a <quote>Helena</quote> varias veces, e vai alguén e lle di que a muller cambiou o nome, e agora se chama <quote>Iria</quote>. En canto sae do teu asombro, decátase de que lle vai tocar substituír todas as aparicións do nome no documento."

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk6 stable6
#: advanced.docbook:479
#, no-c-format
msgid "Enter the command line and issue the command <userinput>%s/Miss Jensen/Ms Jones/</userinput> and hit return, you are done."
msgstr "Acceda á liña de ordes e emita a orde <userinput>%s/Dona Helena/Dona Iria/</userinput>, prema Intro, e listo."

#. Tag: title
#. +> trunk6 stable6
#: advanced.docbook:486
#, no-c-format
msgid "A More Advanced Example"
msgstr "Un exemplo máis avanzado"

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk6 stable6
#: advanced.docbook:488
#, no-c-format
msgid "This example makes use of <emphasis>back references</emphasis> as well as a <emphasis>character class</emphasis> (if you do not know what that is, please refer to the related documentation mentioned below)."
msgstr "O seguinte exemplo usa <emphasis>referencias</emphasis> así como unha <emphasis>clase de caracteres</emphasis> (máis adiante explicarase en que consiste isto)."

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk6 stable6
#: advanced.docbook:493
#, no-c-format
msgid "Suppose you have the following line:"
msgstr "Supoña que ten a seguinte liña:"

#. Tag: programlisting
#. +> trunk6 stable6
#: advanced.docbook:495
#, no-c-format
msgid "void MyClass::DoStringOps( String      &amp;foo, String &amp;bar, String *p, int  &amp;a, int &amp;b )"
msgstr "void UnhaClase::FacerCousas( String      &amp;isto, String &amp;estoutro, String *p, int  &amp;a, int &amp;b )"

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk6 stable6
#: advanced.docbook:497
#, no-c-format
msgid "Now you realize that this is not nice code, and decide that you want to use the <constant>const</constant> keyword for all <quote>address of</quote> arguments, those characterized by the &amp; operator in front of the argument name. You would also like to simplify the white space, so that there is only 1 whitespace character between each word."
msgstr "E de súpeto decátase de que este código é incorrecto de todo, e decide usar a palabra clave <constant>const</constant> para todos os parámetros de <quote>enderezos</quote>, aqueles cuxo nome vai precedido do operador &amp;. Tamén lle gustaría simplificar os espazos, de xeito que só quede un entre cada palabra."

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk6 stable6
#: advanced.docbook:504
#, no-c-format
msgid "Launch the Editing Command Dialog, and enter: <userinput>s/\\s+(\\w+)\\s+(&amp;)/ const \\1 \\2/g</userinput> and hit the <guibutton>OK</guibutton> button. The <userinput>g</userinput> at the end of the expression makes the regular expression recompile for each match to save the <emphasis>backreferences</emphasis>."
msgstr "Inicie o diálogo de ordes de edición, insira <userinput>s/\\s+(\\w+)\\s+(&amp;)/ const \\1 \\2/g</userinput> e prema Intro. O <userinput>g</userinput> ao final da expresión fará que a expresión regular se volva compilar para cada coincidencia, para así gardar as <emphasis>referencias</emphasis>."

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk6 stable6
#: advanced.docbook:509
#, no-c-format
msgid "Output: <computeroutput>void MyClass::DoStringOps( const String &amp;foo, const String &amp;bar, String *p, const int &amp;a, const int &amp;b )</computeroutput>"
msgstr "Resultado: <computeroutput>void UnhaClase::FacerCousas( const String &amp;isto, const String &amp;estoutro, String *p, const int &amp;a, const int &amp;b )</computeroutput>"

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk6 stable6
#: advanced.docbook:513
#, no-c-format
msgid "Mission completed! Now, what happened? Well, we looked for some white space (<literal>\\s+</literal>) followed by one or more alphabetic characters (<literal>\\w+</literal>) followed by some more whitespace (<literal>\\s+</literal>) followed by an ampersand, and in the process saved the alphabetic chunk and the ampersand for reuse in the replace operation. Then we replaced the matching part of our line with one whitespace followed by <quote>const</quote> followed by one whitespace followed by our saved alphabetical chunk (<literal>\\1</literal>) followed by one whitespace followed by our saved ampersand (<literal>\\2</literal>)"
msgstr "Conseguido! Pero que ocorreu? Pois ben, buscamos espazos (<literal>\\s+</literal>) seguidos dun ou máis caracteres latinos de palabras (<literal>\\w+</literal>) seguidos de máis espazos (<literal>\\s+</literal>) seguidos dun «&amp;», e de paso gardamos os caracteres e o «&amp;» para volver usalos no texto de substitución. A continuación substituímos a parte da liña que coincide cun espazo, seguido de <quote>const</quote>, un espazo, a palabra gardada (<literal>\\1</literal>), e o «&amp;» gardado (<literal>\\2</literal>)."

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk6 stable6
#: advanced.docbook:524
#, no-c-format
msgid "Now in some cases the alphabetical chunk was <quote>String</quote>, in some <quote>int</quote>, so using the character class <literal>\\w</literal> and the <literal>+</literal> quantifier proved a valuable asset."
msgstr "Nalgúns casos a palabra gardada foi <quote>String</quote>, noutros <quote>int</quote>, así que fixemos ben en usar a clase de caracteres <literal>\\w</literal> e o cuantificador <literal>+</literal>."

